5. These can be done with twists or to the side to hit the obliques.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Jumping', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Hold an end of the rope in each hand. Position the rope behind you on the ground. Raise vos bras up and turn the rope over votre tête bringing it down in front of you. When it reaches the ground, jump over it. Find a good turning pace that can be maintained. Different speeds and techniques can be used to introduce variation.
2. Rope jumping is exciting, challenges your coordination, and requires a lot of energy. A 150 lb person will burn about 350 calories jumping rope for 30 minutes, compared to over 450 calories running.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Jumping/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Straight-Arm Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope to a high pulley and make your poids selection. Stand a couple feet back from the pulley with vos pieds staggered and take the rope with both hands. Lean forward from the hanche, keeping votre dos straight, with vos bras extended up in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping vos bras straight, extend the épaule to pull the rope down to your cuisses.
3. Pause at the bottom of the motion, squeezing your lats.
4. Revenez en position de départ without allowing the poids to fully rest on the stack.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Straight-Arm_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Round The World Shoulder Stretch', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos jambes together, holding a bodybar or broomstick.
2. Hold the pole behind your hanches with a wider than épaule width grip. Your palms should be down and your thumbs facing out.
3. Lentement, lift vos bras up behind votre tête. Don''t force it if it gets hard to lift further.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Pectoraux. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Round_The_World_Shoulder_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rowing, Stationary', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, seat yourself on the rower. Make sure that your heels are resting comfortably against the base of the foot pedals and that the straps are secured. Select the program that you wish to use, if applicable. Sit up straight and bend forward at the hanches.
2. There are three phases of movement when using a rower. The first phase is when you come forward on the rower. Your genous are bent and against your poitrine. Your upper body is leaning slightly forward while still maintaining good posture. Next, push against the foot pedals and extend vos jambes while bringing vos mains to your upper abdominal area, squeezing your épaules back as you do so. To avoid straining votre dos, use primarily your leg and hanche muscles.
3. The recovery phase simply involves straightening vos bras, bending the genous, and bringing votre corps forward again as you transition back into the first phase.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rowing_Stationary/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Runner''s Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. It''s easiest to get into this stretch if you start standing up, put one leg behind you, and Lentement, lower your torse down to le sol.
2. Keep the front heel on le sol (if it lifts up, scoot your other leg further back).
3. Place vos mains on either side of your front leg. To get more out of this stretch, push your butt up toward the ceiling, and then gradually lower it back toward le sol. You''ll Stretch the hanche flexor of the back leg and the ischio-jambiers and buttocks of the front.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Runners_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Running, Treadmill', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the treadmill and select the desired option from the menu. Most treadmills have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout.
2. Treadmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than running outside. A 150 lb person will burn over 450 calories running 8 miles per hour for 30 minutes. Maintain proper posture as you run, and only hold onto the handles when necessary, such as when dismounting or checking your heart rate.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Running_Treadmill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Russian Twist', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol placing vos pieds either under something that will not move or by having a partner hold them. vos jambes should be bent at the genous.
2. Elevate your upper body so that it creates an imaginary V-shape with your cuisses. vos bras should be fully extended in front of you perpendiculaire à your torse and with the hands clasped. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Twist your torse to the right side until vos bras are parallel with le sol while breathing out.
4. Hold the contraction for a second and move back to the position de départ while breathing out. Now move to the opposite side performing the same techniques you applied to the right side.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Russian_Twist/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sandbag Load', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. To load sandbags or other objects, begin with the implements placed a distance from the loading platform, typically 50 feet.
2. Begin by lifting the sandbag. Sandbags are extremely awkward, and the manner of lifting them can vary depending on the particular sandbag used. Reach as far around it as possible, extending through the hanches and genous to pull it up high. Shouldering is usually not allowed.
3. Move as quickly as possible to the platform, and load it, extending through your hanches, genous, and chevilles to get it as high as possible. Place it onto the platform, ensuring it doesn''t fall off.
4. Revenez en position de départ to retrieve the next sandbag, and Répétez until the event is completed.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Biceps, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sandbag_Load/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Scapular Pull-Up', 'Trapèzes', 'Autre', '1. Take a pronated grip on a pull-up bar.
2. From a hanging position, raise yourself a few inches without using vos bras. Do this by depressing your épaule girdle in a reverse shrugging motion.
3. Pause at the completion of le mouvement, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de départ before performing more repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Scapular_Pull-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Scissor Kick', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, lie down with votre dos pressed against le sol or on an exercise mat (optional). vos bras should be fully extended to the sides with your paumes vers down. Note: The arms should be stationary the entire time.
2. With a slight bend at the genous, lift vos jambes up so that your heels are about 6 inches off the ground. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now lift your left leg up to about a angle de 45 degrés while your right leg is lowered until the heel is about 2-3 inches from the ground.
4. Switch movements by raising your right leg up and lowering your left leg. Remember to breathe while performing cet exercice.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Scissor_Kick/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Scissors Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Assume a lunge stance position with one foot forward with the genou bent, and the rear genou nearly touching the ground.
2. Ensure that the front genou is over the midline of the foot. Extending through both legs, jump as high as possible, swinging vos bras to gain lift.
3. As you jump as high as you can, switch the position of vos jambes, moving your front leg to the back and the rear leg to the front.
4. As you land, absorb the impact through the legs by adopting the lunge position, and Répétez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Scissors_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Band Hamstring Curl', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Secure a band close to the ground and place a banc a couple feet away from it.
2. Seat yourself on the banc and secure the band behind your chevilles, beginning with vos jambes straight. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Flex the genous, bringing vos pieds towards the banc. You may need to lean back slightly to keep vos pieds from striking le sol.
4. Pause at the completion of le mouvement, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Band_Hamstring_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Barbell Military Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Sit on a Military Press banc with a bar behind votre tête and either have a spotter give you the bar (better on the rotator cuff this way) or pick it up yourself carefully with a pronated grip (paumes vers l''avant). Conseil : Your grip should be wider than épaule width and it should create a angle de 90 degrés between the forearm and the upper arm as the barre goes down.
2. Once you pick up the barre with the correct grip length, lift the bar up over votre tête by locking vos bras. Hold at about épaule level and slightly in front of votre tête. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lower the bar down to the collarbone Lentement, as you inspirez.
4. Lift the bar back up to the position de départ as you expirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Barbell_Military_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Barbell Twist', 'Abdominaux', 'Barre', '1. Start out by sitting at the end of a flat banc with a barre placed on top of your cuisses. vos pieds should be épaule width apart from each other.
2. Grip the bar with your paumes vers down and make sure vos mains are wider than épaule width apart from each other. Begin to lift the barre up over votre tête until vos bras are fully extended.
3. Now lower the barre behind votre tête until it is resting along the base of your neck. C''est votre position de départ.
4. While keeping vos pieds and head stationary, move your waist from side to side so that your oblique muscles feel the contraction. Only move from side to side as far as your waist will allow you to go. Stretching or moving too far can cause an injury to occur. Conseil : Use a slow and controlled motion.
5. Remember to Expirez while twisting votre corps to the side and in when moving back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Barbell_Twist/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit down at the end of a flat banc with a haltère in one arm using a neutral grip (palms of the hand facing you).
2. Bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Make sure that you keep the head up.
3. The upper arm with the haltère should be close to the torse and aligned with it (lifted up until it is parallèle au sol while the forearms are pointing towards le sol as the hands hold the poids). Conseil : There should be a angle de 90 degrés between the forearms and the upper arm. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping the upper arm stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids as you expirez until the forearm is parallèle au sol and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.
5. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the haltère back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.
7. Switch arms and Répétez the exercise.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Bent-Over Rear Delt Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Place a couple of haltères looking forward in front of a flat banc.
2. Sit on the end of the banc with vos jambes together and the haltères behind your mollets.
3. Bend at the waist while keeping the back straight in order to pick up the haltères. The palms of vos mains should be facing each other as you pick them. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping your torse forward and stationary, and the arms slightly bent at the coudes, lift the haltères straight to the side until both arms are parallèle au sol. Expirez as you lift the poids. (Note: avoid swinging the torse or bringing the arms back as opposed to the side.)
5. After a one second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the haltères back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_Rear_Delt_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit down at the end of a flat banc with a haltère in both arms using a neutral grip (palms of the hand facing you).
2. Bend your genous slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallèle au sol. Make sure that you keep the head up.
3. The upper arms with the haltères should be close to the torse and aligned with it (lifted up until they are parallèle au sol while the forearms are pointing towards le sol as the hands hold the poids). Conseil : There should be a angle de 90 degrés between the forearms and the upper arm. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids as you expirez until the forearms are parallèle au sol and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves.
5. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the haltères back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Biceps', 'Biceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Asseyez-vous au sol with your genous bent and your partner standing behind you. Extend vos bras straight behind you with your paumes vers each other. Your partner will hold your poignets for you. This will be the position de départ.
2. Attempt to flex your coudes, while your partner prevents any actual movement.
3. After 10-20 seconds, relax vos bras while your partner gently pulls your poignets up to stretch your biceps. Be sure to let your partner know when the stretch is appropriate to prevent injury or overstretching.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Biceps/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Cable Rows', 'Milieu du dos', 'Poulie', '1. For cet exercice you will need access to a low pulley row machine with a V-bar. Note: The V-bar will enable you to have a neutral grip where the palms of vos mains face each other. To get into the position de départ, first sit down on the machine and place vos pieds on the front platform or crossbar provided making sure that your genous are slightly bent and not locked.
2. Lean over as you keep the natural alignment of votre dos and grab the V-bar handles.
3. With vos bras extended pull back until your torse is at a angle de 90 degrés from vos jambes. votre dos should be slightly arched and your poitrine should be sticking out. You should be feeling a nice stretch on your lats as you hold the bar in front of you. C''est votre position de départ. of the exercise.
4. Keeping the torse stationary, pull the handles back towards your torse while keeping the arms close to it until you touch the abdominals. Expirez as you perform that movement. At that point you should be squeezing votre dos muscles hard. Hold that contraction for a second and Lentement, go back to the original position while breathing in.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Cable_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Cable Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Adjust the poids to an appropriate amount and be seated, grasping the handles. Your upper arms should be about 90 degrees to the body, with votre tête and poitrine up. The coudes should also be bent to about 90 degrees. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by extending through the coude, pressing the handles together above votre tête.
3. After pausing at the top, return the handles to the position de départ. Ensure that you maintain tension on the cables.
4. You can also execute this movement with votre dos off the pad and alternate hands.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Cable_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Sit on the machine and place your toes on the lower portion of the platform provided with the heels extending off. Choose the toe positioning of your choice (forward, in, or out) as per the beginning of this chapter.
2. Place your lower cuisses under the lever pad, which will need to be adjusted according to the height of your cuisses. Now place vos mains on top of the lever pad in order to prevent it from slipping forward.
3. Lift the lever slightly by pushing your heels up and release the safety bar. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lentement, lower your heels by bending at the chevilles until the mollets are fully stretched. Inspirez as you perform this movement.
5. Raise the heels by extending the chevilles as high as possible as you contract the mollets and Expirez. Hold the top contraction for a second.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Calf Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Sit up straight on an exercise mat.
2. Bend one genou and put that foot on le sol to stabilize the torse.
3. Straighten your other leg and flex your cheville.
4. Using a band, towel, or your hand if you can reach, pull the toes toward you. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds, then switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Close-Grip Concentration Barbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Sit down on a flat banc with a barre or E-Z Bar in front of you in between vos jambes. vos jambes should be spread with the genous bent and the feet on le sol.
2. Use vos bras to pick the barre up and place the back of your upper arms on top of your inner cuisses (around three and a half inches away from the front of the genou). A supinated grip closer than épaule width is needed to perform cet exercice. Conseil : Your arm should be extended bras tendus and the barre should be above le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps.
4. Lentement, begin to bring the barre back to position de départ as your Inspirez. Conseil : Avoid swinging motions at any time.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Close-Grip_Concentration_Barbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on a flat banc with a haltère on each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse.
2. Rotate the palms of the hands so that they are facing your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the poids and start twisting the poignets once the haltères pass your cuisses so that the palms of vos mains face forward at the end of le mouvement. Make sure that you contract the biceps as you Expirez and make sure that only the forearms move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps.
4. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back to the position de départ as your Inspirez and as you rotate the poignets back to a neutral grip.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Inner Biceps Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on the end of a flat banc with a haltère in each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse.
2. Rotate the palms of the hands so that they are facing inward in a neutral position. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the haltères out and up, turning the palms out as you lift and keeping your forearms in line with your outer deltoids. Tips:
4. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps.
5. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back to the position de départ as your Inspirez. Remember to rotate vos bras as you lower the haltères so that you can switch back to a neutral grip.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Inner_Biceps_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Palms-Down Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Start out by placing two haltères on le sol in front of a flat banc.
2. Sit down on the edge of the flat banc with vos jambes at about épaule width apart. Make sure to keep vos pieds on le sol.
3. Use vos bras to grab both of the haltères and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against your cuisses with the palms of the hands facing down. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge of your cuisses.
4. Start out by curling your poignet upwards and exhaling.
5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de départ while inhaling. Make sure to inspirez during this part of the exercise. Conseil : Your forearms should be stationary as your poignet is the only movement needed to perform cet exercice.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
7. When finished, simply lower the haltères to le sol.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Palms-Up Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Start out by placing two haltères on le sol in front of a flat banc.
2. Sit down on the edge of the flat banc with vos jambes at about épaule width apart. Make sure to keep vos pieds on le sol.
3. Use vos bras to grab both of the haltères and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against your cuisses with the palms of the hands facing up. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge of your cuisses.
4. Start out by curling your poignet upwards and exhaling.
5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de départ while inhaling. Make sure to inspirez during this part of the exercise. Conseil : Your forearms should be stationary as your poignet is the only movement needed to perform cet exercice.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
7. When finished, simply lower the haltères to le sol.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Palms-Up_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a couple of haltères and sit on a military press banc or a utility banc that has a back support on it as you place the haltères upright on top of your cuisses.
2. Clean the haltères up one at a time by using your cuisses to bring the haltères up to épaule height at each side.
3. Rotate the poignets so that the palms of vos mains are facing forward. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you expirez, push the haltères up until they touch at the top.
5. Après une pause, Lentement, come down back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Flat Bench Leg Pull-In', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc with the legs stretched out in front of you slightly below parallel and vos bras holding on to the sides of the banc. Your torse should be leaning backwards around a angle de 45 degrés from the banc. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Bring the genous in toward you as you move your torse closer to them at the same time. Expirez as you perform this movement.
3. Après une pause, go back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Flat_Bench_Leg_Pull-In/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Floor Hamstring Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Sit on a mat with your right leg extended in front of you and your left leg bent with your foot against your right inner cuisse.
2. Lean forward from your hanches and reach for your cheville until you feel a stretch in your ischio-jambiers. Maintenez 15- secondes, then Répétez for your other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Floor_Hamstring_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Front Deltoid', 'Épaules', 'Poids de corps', '1. Sit upright on le sol with vos jambes bent, your partner standing behind you. Stick vos bras straight out to your sides, with your paumes vers the ground. Attempt to move them as far behind you as possible, as your assistant holds your poignets. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping your coudes straight, attempt to move vos bras to the front, with your partner gently restraining you to prevent any actual movement for 10-20 seconds.
3. Now, relax your muscles and allow your partner to gently increase the stretch on the épaules and poitrine. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Front_Deltoid/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Glute', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. In a seated position with your genous bent, cross one cheville over the opposite genou. Your partner will stand behind you. Now, lean forward as your partner braces your épaules with their hands. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Attempt to push your torse back for 10-20 seconds, as your partner prevents any actual movement of your torse.
3. Now relax your muscles as your partner increases the stretch by gently pushing your torse forward for 10-20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Glute/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Good Mornings', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. Set up a box in a power rack. The pins should be set at an appropriate height. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the épaules, not on top of your traps. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your épaules.
2. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back. Keep votre tête facing forward. With votre dos, épaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genous and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hanches until you are seated on the box. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Keeping the bar tight, bend forward at the hanches as much as possible. If you set the pins to what would be parallel, you not only have a safety if you fail, but know when to stop.
4. Pause just above the pins and reverse the motion until your torse it upright.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Good_Mornings/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Hamstring', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. In a seated position with vos jambes extended, have your partner stand behind you. Now, lean forward as your partner braces your épaules with their hands. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Attempt to push your torse back for 10-20 seconds, as your partner prevents any actual movement of your torse.
3. Now relax your muscles as your partner increases the stretch by gently pushing your torse forward for 10-20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Hamstring/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Hamstring and Calf Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Loop a belt, rope, or band around one foot. Sit down with both legs extended . C''est votre position de départ.
2. Leaning forward slightly, pull on the belt to draw the toes of your foot back. Hold this position for 10-20 seconds and then Répétez with the other leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Hamstring_and_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Head Harness Neck Resistance', 'Cou', 'Autre', '1. Place a neck strap on le sol at the end of a flat banc. Once you have selected the poids, sit at the end of the flat banc with vos pieds wider than épaule width apart from each other. Your toes should be pointed out.
2. Lentement, move your torse forward until it is almost parallel with le sol. Using both hands, securely position the neck strap around votre tête. Conseil : Make sure the poids are still lying on le sol to prevent any strain on the neck. Now grab the poids with both hands while elevating your torse back until it is almost perpendiculaire à le sol. Note: votre tête and torse needs to be slightly tilted forward to perform cet exercice.
3. Now place both hands on top of your genous. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lentement, lower your neck down until your chin touches the upper part of your poitrine while breathing in.
5. While exhaling, bring your neck back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Head_Harness_Neck_Resistance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Leg Curl', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the machine lever to fit your height and sit on the machine with votre dos against the back support pad.
2. Place the back of lower leg on top of padded lever (just a few inches under the mollets) and secure the lap pad against your cuisses, just above the genous. Then grasp the side handles on the machine as you point your toes straight (or you can also use any of the other two stances) and ensure that the legs are fully straight right in front of you. C''est votre position de départ.
3. As you expirez, pull the machine lever as far as possible to the back of your cuisses by flexing at the genous. Keep your torse stationary en permanence. Maintenez la position 1 seconde.
4. Lentement, Revenez en position de départ as you Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Leg_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Leg Tucks', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc with the legs stretched out in front of you slightly below parallel and vos bras holding on to the sides of the banc. Your torse should be leaning backwards around a angle de 45 degrés from the banc. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Bring the genous in toward you as you move your torse closer to them at the same time. Expirez as you perform this movement.
3. Après une pause, go back to the position de départ as you inspirez.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Leg_Tucks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Down Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on a flat banc with a haltère in your right hand.
2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than épaule width apart.
3. Lean forward and place your right forearm on top of your upper right cuisse with your palm down. Conseil : Make sure that the back of the poignet lies on top of your genous. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lower the haltère as far as possible as you keep a tight grip on the haltère. Inspirez as you perform this movement.
5. Now curl the haltère as high as possible as you contract the forearms and as you expirez. Keep the contraction for a second before you lower again. Conseil : The only movement should happen at the poignet.
6. Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions, switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Up Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on a flat banc with a haltère in your right hand.
2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than épaule width apart.
3. Lean forward and place your right forearm on top of your upper right cuisse with your palm up. Conseil : Make sure that the front of the poignet lies on top of your genous. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lower the haltère as far as possible as you keep a tight grip on the haltère. Inspirez as you perform this movement.
5. Now curl the haltère as high as possible as you contract the forearms and as you expirez. Keep the contraction for a second before you lower again. Conseil : The only movement should happen at the poignet.
6. Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions, switch arms and Répétez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Palms-Up_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated One-arm Cable Pulley Rows', 'Milieu du dos', 'Poulie', '1. To get into the position de départ, first sit down on the machine and place vos pieds on the front platform or crossbar provided making sure that your genous are slightly bent and not locked.
2. Lean over as you keep the natural alignment of votre dos and grab the single handle attachment with your left arm using a palms-down grip.
3. With your arm extended pull back until your torse is at a angle de 90 degrés from vos jambes. votre dos should be slightly arched and your poitrine should be sticking out. You should be feeling a nice stretch on your lat as you hold the bar in front of you. The right arm can be kept by the waist. C''est votre position de départ. of the exercise.
4. Keeping the torse stationary, pull the handles back towards your torse while keeping the arms close to it as you rotate the poignet, so that by the time your hand is by your abdominals it is in a neutral position (paumes vers the torse). Expirez as you perform that movement. At that point you should be squeezing votre dos muscles hard.
5. Hold that contraction for a second and Lentement, go back to the original position while breathing in. Conseil : Remember to rotate the poignet as you go back to the position de départ so that the palms are facing down again.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. and then perform the same movement with the right hand.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_One-arm_Cable_Pulley_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Overhead Stretch', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Sit up straight on an exercise mat.
2. Touch the soles of vos pieds together with vos pieds six to eight inches in front of your hanches.
3. Place one hand on le sol beside you and your other hand behind votre tête.
4. Lift your coude to the ceiling as you incline your torse to the other side. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds, then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Overhead_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Palm-Up Barbell Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands and your paumes vers up; hands spaced about épaule width.
2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than épaule width apart.
3. Lean forward and place your forearms on top of your upper cuisses with your palms up. Conseil : Make sure that the front of the poignets lay on top of your genous. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lower the bar as far as possible while inhaling and keeping a tight grip.
5. Now curl bar up as high as possible while flexing the forearms and exhaling. Hold the contraction at the top for a second and Conseil : Only the poignet should move.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Palm-Up_Barbell_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Palms-Down Barbell Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands and your paumes vers down; hands spaced about épaule width.
2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than épaule width apart.
3. Lean forward and place your forearms on top of your upper cuisses with your palms down. Conseil : Make sure that the back of the poignets lay on top of your genous. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Lower the bar as far as possible while inhaling and keeping a tight grip.
5. Now curl bar up as high as possible while flexing the forearms and exhaling. Hold the contraction at the top for a second and Conseil : Only the poignet should move.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Palms-Down_Barbell_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Side Lateral Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Pick a couple of haltères and sit at the end of a flat banc with vos pieds firmly on le sol. Hold the haltères with your paumes vers in and vos bras straight down at your sides at arms'' length. C''est votre position de départ.
